[finding.7.1.8-follower-two-pass-pointers]
revision = 5e4195600
command = go test -count=1 ./services/platform/perps-data/internal/source/ -run TestFollower
exit = 1
log = fleet/logs/release-7.1.8-follower-1.log
observed = Ten of eleven follower subtests pass including the new prefetch ordering test; two_pass_pointers fails at its own precondition search for a ShareTokenCreated log with a same-block Transfer because the throwaway chain was never seeded with a share token, before any follower code runs.
assumption = The subtest is run once on a chain seeded with a share token at the wave gate; the follower test harness is not part of the task verify.

[finding.7.3.5-latency-on-quiet-host]
revision = 956321582
command = go test -count=1 ./services/platform/perps-data/loadtest/ -run 'TestLoadProfile'
exit = 1
log = fleet/logs/release-7.3.5-fix-verify-4.log
observed = On a host at load average 11 on 18 cores the storm guard held again but the p99 frame delay measured 48.8 s against the 250 ms bound with late checksums, so the remaining failure is a code defect of the frame path and not host load.
assumption = The earlier host-load assumption is withdrawn; the frame path is profiled and fixed before 7.3.5 is marked done.

[finding.2.3.99-pre-existing-failures]
revision = 82e5ab6bc
command = go test ./modules/launchpad/... ./precompiles/launchpad/...
exit = 1
log = fleet/logs/release-2.3.99-verify-5.log
observed = TestLaunchpadDomainWiring and every test of launchpadtest, types, the v610 legacy keeper and types and the v610 legacy precompile pass; modules/launchpad/keeper fails TestAirdropHoldingHistory with LXP_LAUNCHPAD_INVALID_GENESIS fee account disagrees with market, and precompiles/launchpad fails TestOpticalHooksSeeTheContractCallers and aborts on a nil pointer dereference in TestCallKindRefusals, none of which the task touches.
assumption = The three failures are fixed in their own packages and the task verify is taken once more on the merged revision before 2.3.99 is marked done.

[finding.2.3.99-precompile-tests-fixed]
revision = 2ae1f8152
command = go test ./precompiles/launchpad/...
exit = 0
log = fleet/logs/release-2.3.99-precompile-verify-2.log
observed = TestCallKindRefusals dereferenced nil because the run test env built the keeper without an EVM keeper after InitGenesis began installing the generation 2 role surfaces through it; the env now mounts an EVM store and passes a real EVM keeper as events_test does, and TestOpticalHooksSeeTheContractCallers passes once LAUNCHPAD_CONTRACTS_DIR points at launchpad/contracts/contracts and SOLC at a 0.8.24-compatible solc.
assumption = Every run of the launchpad precompile tests sets those two variables; the test code is unchanged.

[finding.7.3.5-double-tape-read]
revision = 77e1b4332
command = go test -count=1 ./services/platform/perps-data/loadtest/ -run 'TestLoadProfile'
exit = 1
log = fleet/logs/release-7.3.5-latency-verify-1.log
observed = Each fill's tape was read from the database twice, once under the hub lock at about 35 ms prepare plus 17 ms locked per message against a 28 ms budget, and the gateway churned Postgres connections with a two-connection idle pool; with the prefetched items reused, prepare parallel per family and 64 idle connections the p99 frame delay fell from 48.8 s to 2.27 s with zero late checksums, zero gaps and zero server closes, still above 250 ms.
assumption = The remaining delay is measured from the fill's block time stamped before the trader's own transaction and eighteen serial publishes while the box answered SELECT 1 in 80 ms to 3 s; the gate is rerun once with no other build on the box, and if it still fails the ramp and storm subscribe contention on the hub lock is the next target.
